mber","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:17:26-07:00","id":1395363,"title":"","content":"As much as I would love it, I lack money and friends to justify myself to be a VR device. Honestly from my opinion the whole VR thing is a bit like the PS Vita. In theory awesome, in practice the whole lack of exclusive only games for it is not enough to invest in one and because of the lack of such in the consumer base no one is really wanting to develop something to such a niche.<br /> As far as I knew the whole big VR games are either just adaptions of other big PC games like Skyrim or got patched to work without VR like ST Bridge Crew. I am honestly skeptical if Wr Afterlive would change something because VR lacks a killer feature to justify people paying 400-600\u20ac for playing one game like Halo V for X1 or FF VII for PS4.<br /> <br /> I give this game if it is realeased VR only a year until it either get changed to PC working too or wrote of as buiseness failure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:24:19-07:00","id":1395368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalkSam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1395167-wraith-the-oblivion-afterlife-announced?p=1395261#post1395261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would it not be?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1349602-orpheus-5th\">This here. </a><br /> <br /> Basically, seeing that trademark lead people to the assumption that a.) not only that there would be an &quot;Orpheus 5e&quot; but that b.) because there was no direct evidence at that time time suggest that a Wraith 5e was being considered (especially post-V5 controversies), c.) knowing that Wraith wasn't warmly received when it first released, people made the jump that Orpheus would become WoD5e's primary &quot;ghost game&quot;. Therefore, there would be no Wraith 5e.<br /> <br /> Although, now that the idea of there being an update to Wraith and Orpheus existing alongside each other in the same edition, now the possibilities are there for more deliberate crossover between the two...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-09T09:34:41-07:00","id":1395375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.yout